{"id":"96a3f205-3a6d-4da2-8041-d792e5056ba7","object":"chat.completion","created":1785019774,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    required_symbols = case['required_symbols']\\n    node_map = {n['id']: n for n in nodes}\\n    children_map = {n['id']: [] for n in nodes}\\n    root_id = None\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        p = n.get('parent')\\n        if p is None:\\n            root_id = n['id']\\n        else:\\n            children_map[p].append(n['id'])\\n    retained = set(node_map.keys())\\n    from collections import Counter\\n    counts = Counter(n['symbol'] for n in nodes)\\n    removed = []\\n    order = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n['depth'], n['id']))\\n    for n in order:\\n        nid = n['id']\\n        if nid not in retained:\\n            continue\\n        if nid == root_id:\\n            continue\\n        if not n['removable']:\\n            continue\\n        if any(child in retained for child in children_map.get(nid, [])):\\n            continue\\n        sym = n['symbol']\\n        counts[sym] -= 1\\n        if all(counts[req] >= 1 for req in required_symbols):\\n            retained.remove(nid)\\n            removed.append(nid)\\n        else:\\n            counts[sym] += 1\\n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\\n    return {'removed_node_ids': removed, 'retained_node_ids': retained_sorted}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that returns removed_node_ids and retained_node_ids based on the given payload. The task is about grammar-guided node reduction, similar to Perses reduction. The payload contains nodes with id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility. There is also required_symbols list.\n\nThe goal: given a tree (root at depth 0 with parent null), we want to remove some nodes while preserving that all required_symbols are represented somewhere in the retained tree. Also, we cann